  Placement: 1
  CardStory: "He reminisces on what happened on the walls, lying on his bed in the
    barracks. Did last night really happen?\r\n\r\n*Yes, the temperature was low.*
    2Spade blinks and frowns. Is that what he should be focusing on? *Yes. It is.*
    But was that the problem? 2Spade isn\u2019t sure, and everyone else seems to
    have forgotten. And there are a lot of people here.\r\n\r\n*Most bunks are occupied,
    which makes sense. Each soldier has a bunk. But there is an empty one next to
    mine. Why is it empty? Bunks should have soldiers in them. I remember the soldier
    who used to be there.* \r\n\r\nThe bunk is there, but when 2Spade asks the others
    about him, no one knows what *I am talking about.* 2Spade is told it was never
    occupied. He thinks they are right, he knows there was never a soldier there.
    *But there must have been. All soldiers are assigned a bunk. I just can\u2019t
    remember what his face looked like.*"
